<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 10-JAN.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 10-JAN.</headline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Cyclone Drena has 50 mph winds and is in the Tasmanian Sea near 37s/171e, moving southeast at 17 mph. Drena is now an extratropical storm. It still is somewhat of a risk to shipping due to gusty winds and rough seas. It will also bring locally heavy rain and wind to New Zealand as it tracks into that area in about 12-24 hours.  </p>
<p>THERE ARE NO FURTHER EMERGENCY WEATHER STATEMENTS</p>
</text>
